    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score (82.62) against Rocker. With a strong platoon advantage and the top spot in the lineup, **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear must-start. We are also leaning heavily into our outfield depth, as **Kyle Tucker** (77.45) and **Andy Pages** (75.63) both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Rodriguez, whose 4.82 xERA invites high-upside production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** rounds out our elite tier at 74.56, benefiting from a high-leverage cleanup spot and a strong platoon edge against Holmes.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Coby Mayo**, whose 46.48 projection fell just short of our daily threshold. While he shares the same favorable matchup as **Gunnar Henderson**, his position in the bottom third of the order, combined with a negative platoon variance, relegated him to the bench in favor of our higher-efficiency infielders. Meanwhile, we remain wary of the matchups facing **Drake Baldwin** (48.97) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.16); both are fighting through suboptimal SP pairings, with **Drake Baldwin** facing a stiff 2.91 xERA challenge from Schlittler. We are also monitoring the SB potential closely; while **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** face pitchers with high hold rates, their positional versatility and order placement keep them firmly in the green. Ensure all eyes remain on the lineup wire, as any late defensive replacements for **Jacob Wilson** or **Wade Meckler** could necessitate a quick pivot to preserve our remaining game caps.",
